{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"brown-caring-weasel","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# Context\n\nGerrit 1658 (bug 79d6) took a spurious `Verified -1` on run 31626336603: `1 failed, 12327 passed` on macos-latest/py3.13, in a file the change does not touch.\n\nFailure: `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/orchestrate/test_reconcile_main.py::test_main_without_repo_root_passes_resolved_repo_root` — `AssertionError: check_pass_lock must be called when main() runs (assert 0 >= 1)`.\n\n# Mechanism (confirmed from source + job log)\n\nThe test deliberately `monkeypatch.delenv(\"REBAR_ROOT\")` so the genuine depth-fallback (`Path(__file__).resolve().parents[4]`) resolves the REAL repo root — that resolution is the thing under test. It then patches `check_pass_lock`/`check_phase_gate`/`acquire_pass_lock`/`release_pass_lock` and asserts `check_pass_lock` was called.\n\nBut in `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/__main__.py`, `_pause_exit_code()` runs BEFORE `_post_pause_preflight()` — and `_post_pause_preflight` is what calls `check_pass_lock`. `_pause_exit_code` calls `advisory.read_pause(repo_root)` against that real repo root, and on `ReconcileGateError` returns early (`__main__.py:171`). The job log carries exactly that message at the failure: `ERROR: refs/reconciler/gate is corrupt; run 'rebar bridge resume' to clear it`.\n\nSo with a corrupt/unreadable `refs/reconciler/gate` in the runner checkout, `main()` returns before `check_pass_lock`, and the assertion fails through no fault of the patch under test. `read_pause` is NOT mocked, unlike every other advisory call in the test. The file passes locally (13 passed).\n\n# Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1 — The test no longer depends on the real repo's `refs/reconciler/gate` state: `read_pause` is stubbed (or the gate ref is isolated) so a corrupt/leftover ref cannot make it fail, while the repo-root RESOLUTION assertion it exists for is preserved.\n- [ ] AC2 — A regression check demonstrates the test passes with a deliberately corrupt gate ref present.\n- [ ] AC3 — Any sibling test in the file that clears `REBAR_ROOT` and leaves an advisory call unmocked gets the same treatment (audit, and state the result).","id":"b82c-7461-0d95-44b8","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Reconciler main test reads real repo gate ref; corrupt ref flakes CI"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786560571313071001,"uuid":"5a415367-42b3-4e01-a289-afc003372e75"}